A React component re-renders when you pass an inline object as a prop because **each render creates a new object reference**, and React uses reference equality (not value equality) to detect prop changes.

## The Problem

```jsx
function Parent() {
  return <Child config={{ timeout: 5000 }} />;
}

function Child({ config }) {
  console.log("Child rendered");
  return <div>{config.timeout}</div>;
}
```

Every time `Parent` renders, `{ timeout: 5000 }` is a **new object in memory**. Even though its *value* is identical, it's a different reference (`{}` !== `{}`). React's default shallow equality check sees this as a prop change, so `Child` re-renders unnecessarily.

## Why This Happens

React's reconciliation algorithm uses:
- **Reference equality** for objects and arrays (`a === b`)
- **Value equality** for primitives

This is by design for performance — deep equality checks would be expensive.

## Solutions

**1. Move the object outside the component (best for static data)**
```jsx
const CONFIG = { timeout: 5000 };

function Parent() {
  return <Child config={CONFIG} />;
}
```

**2. Memoize with `useMemo`**
```jsx
function Parent() {
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ timeout: 5000 }), []);
  return <Child config={config} />;
}
```

**3. Memoize the child component with `memo`**
```jsx
const Child = memo(function Child({ config }) {
  return <div>{config.timeout}</div>;
});
```

**4. Split into primitive props**
```jsx
function Parent() {
  return <Child timeout={5000} />;
}
```

**Best practice:** Use option 1 or 4 when possible. Only reach for `useMemo` when the object needs dynamic values or dependencies.

# Todo App REST API Design

## Data Model

```typescript
interface Todo {
  id: string;              // UUID
  title: string;           // 1-255 chars
  description?: string;    // Optional
  completed: boolean;      // Default: false
  dueDate?: string;        // ISO 8601 date
  priority: "low" | "medium" | "high";  // Default: medium
  createdAt: string;       // ISO timestamp
  updatedAt: string;       // ISO timestamp
}

interface CreateTodoRequest {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  dueDate?: string;
  priority?: "low" | "medium" | "high";
}

interface UpdateTodoRequest {
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  completed?: boolean;
  dueDate?: string;
  priority?: "low" | "medium" | "high";
}
```

## Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| `GET` | `/todos` | List all todos (with optional filters: `?completed=true`, `?priority=high`) |
| `GET` | `/todos/:id` | Get single todo |
| `POST` | `/todos` | Create todo |
| `PATCH` | `/todos/:id` | Update todo |
| `DELETE` | `/todos/:id` | Delete todo |
| `PUT` | `/todos/:id/toggle` | Toggle completion status |
| `DELETE` | `/todos` | Delete all completed todos |

